"""Central stages 4–33, with separate textual contexts and commentary evidence."""


def R(slug, name, en_name, cn, en, note):
    return dict(slug=slug, name=name, en_name=en_name, description=cn, en_quote=en, en_description=en + ' ' + note, en_note=note)


ROWS = [
R('r01-conglong','葱聾','Mount Conglong','渠豬向东三十五里至葱聾，多大谷、白垩与黑青黄垩。郭注杂色垩，各色分录但不擅定现代矿种；与次五同名山分开。','Thirty-five li east is Mount Conglong, with great valleys and white, black, blue-green and yellow e.','The commentary calls these mixed-color e; color terms do not establish modern mineral species. The later same-name mountain remains separate.'),
R('r01-wo','涹山','Mount Wo','葱聾向东十五里为涹山，上多赤铜、阴多铁。保留上与阴的原文位置，不把阴改成另一条路线或现代矿带。','Fifteen li east is Mount Wo, with much red copper above and iron on its shaded side.','The mountain-name pronunciation is compared to wo; no modern mineral mapping is inferred.'),
R('r01-tuohu','脱扈','Mount Tuohu','涹向东七十里为脱扈。植楮草葵叶赤华荚实、实如㯶荚；㯶荚似皂荚为郭注比较，不移作植楮同一物种。癙病注文跨17—18，食不眯为古述。','Seventy li east is Mount Tuohu. Zhichu has mallow-like leaves, red flowers and pods resembling zong pods; it is said to relieve shu illness and avert harmful bewilderment when eaten.','Units 16–18 are all on scan 3. The zong-pod comparison and the shu gloss remain distinct; the latter continues across 17–18.'),
R('r01-jinxing','金星','Mount Jinxing','向东二十里为金星，多天嬰，状如龙骨，可已痤为古述。正文未定天嬰所属草木、动物或矿物，作为未定类别物产存名，不生成龙形生物。','Twenty li east is Mount Jinxing, with much Tianying, compared to dragon bones and said to relieve sores.','The product category is not supplied. A dragon-bone comparison does not add a dragon creature or identify a modern medicine.'),
R('r01-taiwei','泰威','Mount Taiwei','向东七十里为泰威，有梟谷、多铁。郭注或无谷字为文本异说，不把梟谷画成枭鸟或新增山段。','Seventy li east is Mount Taiwei, with a valley called Xiao and abundant iron.','The commentary notes a variant without the valley character; the place name supplies no owl anatomy.'),
R('r01-jianggu','橿谷','Mount Jianggu','向东十五里为橿谷，多赤铜；郭注或作檀谷之山，山名异说分存，不与歴兒橿木相混。','Fifteen li east is Mount Jianggu, with much red copper.','Tangu is a commentary variant of the mountain name, not an additional route mountain.'),
R('r01-wulin','吳林','Mount Wulin','向东百二十里为吳林，多葌草。郭注亦菅字，仅释写法，不借葌山芒草赤叶补本段草形。','A hundred and twenty li east is Mount Wulin, with abundant jian grass.','Guo Pu identifies a character variant; no anatomy is borrowed from the later Jian mountain tree.'),
R('r01-niushou','牛首','Mount Niushou','吳林向北三十里为牛首，鬼草葵叶赤茎、秀如禾。劳水西注潏水，多飞鱼如鲋；不因飞名添翼，不混騩山豚状赤文飞鱼。鬼字仅在阅读层恢复，捕获保留缺字图。','Thirty li north is Mount Niushou. Gui grass has mallow-like leaves, red stems and grain-like shoots and is said to avert worry. Lao water flows west into the Yu and has Feiyu resembling fu fish, with an ancient eating claim.','Guo Pu explicitly leaves the proposed contemporary Niushou identification uncertain. The flying-fish name supplies no wings; the captured missing-image marker remains unchanged.'),
R('r01-huo','霍山','Mount Huo','向北四十里为霍山，多榖。朏朏狸状白尾有鬣，蓄养已忧为古述。郭注列举多地霍山并称以霍为名者非一，不指定现代唯一坐标。','Forty li north is Mount Huo, with many gu trees. Feifei resembles a li with a white tail and a mane; keeping it is said to relieve worry.','The long Huo-name commentary spans 29–30 and describes multiple namesakes. Four feline feet, mane styling, other colors and pose are artistic.'),
R('r01-hegu','合谷','Mount Hegu','向北五十二里为合谷，多薝棘。郭注未詳音瞻，只录名和不确定性，不据棘字强定现代植物。','Fifty-two li north is Mount Hegu, with much zhanji.','Guo Pu says it is not known and gives a pronunciation gloss; the thorn character does not identify a modern plant.'),
R('r01-yin','隂山','Mount Yin','向北三十五里为隂山，多砺石文石。少水出焉是水名，不把少字误解为缺水。彫棠叶如榆而方、实如赤菽；食疗为古述。','Thirty-five li north is Mount Yin, with li and patterned stones. Shao water rises here. Diaotang has square elm-like leaves and fruit like red beans and is said to relieve deafness when eaten.','Xian mountain is a name variant in commentary. Shao is a water name, not a statement that water is scarce.'),
R('r01-gudeng','皷鐙','Mount Gudeng','向东北四百里为皷鐙，多赤铜。榮草柳叶、本如鸡卵，食之已风为古述；36在5页末，不把行程拆给另一山。','Four hundred li northeast is Mount Gudeng, with much red copper. Rong grass has willow-like leaves and an egg-like base and is said to relieve wind illness when eaten.','Unit 36 is at the end of scan 5, with 37 on scan 6. The base comparison supplies no chicken creature or exact size.'),
R('r01-summary','首列总括','First-range summary and rites','首列甘棗至皷鐙，十五山六千六百七十里照录。歴兒冢、太牢吉玉与余十三山一羊桑封等分存，不把十五减一与十三的差异擅补。桑封方下锐上中穿、加金为神主礼制，无统一神形记载。','The first range from Ganzao to Gudeng is stated to contain fifteen mountains and 6,670 li. Li-er has a distinguished rite; the other thirteen mountains use one sheep and a buried sangfeng tablet, without grain.','The reported numbers remain even where their relationship is unclear. The mulberry tablet has a square lower part, pointed upper part, a central hole and metal decoration; these are ritual details, not deity anatomy.'),
R('r02-huizhu','煇諸','Mount Huizhu','中次二济山首煇諸，多桑、閭麋和鶡。閭麋泛称分录留占位；鶡郭注雉状而大、青色有毛，据注作图，不移用现代精确种属。','The second Central range begins at Mount Huizhu, with mulberry trees, lu and mi animals, and He birds.','The He form comes from commentary: pheasant-like, large and blue-green feathered. The animal names alone do not identify their modern species.'),
R('r02-fashi','發視','Mount Fashi','煇諸向西南二百里为發視，上多金玉、下多砥砺；即鱼水西注伊水。即鱼在此是水名一部分，不另造即鱼生物。','Two hundred li southwest is Mount Fashi, with gold and jade above and di and li stones below. Jiyu water flows west into the Yi.','Unit 45 is on scan 6, followed by 46 on 7. Jiyu is the water name here, not a newly described fish.'),
R('r02-hao','豪山','Mount Hao','向西三百里为豪山，多金玉而无草木；不因与豪鱼同字添加鱼类、河流或植被。','Three hundred li west is Mount Hao, with much gold and jade but no vegetation.','The mountain and the earlier Hao fish are distinct names and records.'),
R('r02-xian','鮮山','Mount Xian','向西三百里为鮮山，多金玉、无草木。鲜水北注伊水，鸣蛇蛇状四翼、磬声；四翼须可数，旱兆为古述。','Three hundred li west is Mount Xian, with gold and jade but no vegetation. Xian water flows north into the Yi and has Ming snakes: snake-shaped with four wings and a sound like a chime stone, with an ancient drought omen.','Four separate wings are mandatory; wing type, placement, colors and snake posture are artistic.'),
R('r02-yang','陽山','Mount Yang','向西三百里为陽山，多石、无草木。阳水北注伊水，化蛇人面豺身鸟翼而蛇行；蛇行是行动比拟，不等于蛇尾或蛇躯，洪水兆为古述。','Three hundred li west is Mount Yang, with much stone but no vegetation. Yang water flows north into the Yi. Huashe has a human face, jackal body and bird wings, moves like a snake and is said to herald floods.','Snake-like movement does not state a serpent tail. Limb count, wing pair, colors and low posture in the image are artistic.'),
R('r02-kunwu','昆吾','Mount Kunwu','向西二百里为昆吾，多赤铜。铜剑长郭注跨54—57，蠪蚳彘状有角、号哭声；本段不借西山同名人面羊角形，功效为古述。','Two hundred li west is Mount Kunwu, with much red copper. Longchi resembles a pig with horns, sounds like human wailing and has an ancient eating claim.','The copper-and-sword commentary spans 54–57. The pig form stays separate from the Western same-name creature; horn count and styling are artistic.'),
R('r02-jian','葌山','Mount Jian','向西百二十里为葌山，葌水北注伊水，上金玉、下青雄黄。芒草虽名草而正文称木，棠状赤叶、可毒鱼；按树木记述，不并吳林葌草。','A hundred and twenty li west is Mount Jian. Jian water flows north into the Yi; gold and jade occur above and green xionghuang below. Mangcao is explicitly a tree resembling tang, with red leaves and an ancient fish-poisoning claim.','Its name does not override the main text calling it a tree. No poisoning instructions or modern species determination are added.'),
R('r02-dusu','獨蘇','Mount Dusu','向西一百五十里为獨蘇，无草木而多水。只录无名水文，不捏造出水名称、流向或神兽。','A hundred and fifty li west is Mount Dusu, without vegetation and with much water.','No named river, recipient or individual creature is supplied.'),
R('r02-manqu','蔓渠','Mount Manqu','向西二百里为蔓渠，上多金玉、下多竹箭。伊水出而东注洛，古地理注不作现代实测；马腹人面虎身、婴儿音、食人为古述。','Two hundred li west is Mount Manqu, with gold and jade above and arrow bamboo below. The Yi rises here and flows east into the Luo. Mafu has a human face and tiger body, sounds like an infant and is described as eating people.','Unit 63 is on scan 8, followed by 64–66 on 9. The Yi geographic gloss continues into 65; infant sound does not require an infant face or a violent scene.'),
R('r02-summary','次二总括','Second-range summary and rites','次二煇諸至蔓渠，九山一千六百七十里。神人面鸟身；祭毛择色、用一吉玉投而不糈。正文未指定牲种，不补鸡羊，也不画成人身长翼代替鸟身。','The second range from Huizhu to Manqu contains nine mountains and 1,670 li. Its gods have human faces and bird bodies. The rite selects fur color and uses one auspicious jade, cast in, without grain.','The offering species is not specified. A human face and full bird body do not describe a winged human torso.'),
R('r03-aoan','敖岸','Mount Ao-an','中次三萯山首敖岸，阳㻬琈玉、阴赭黄金，熏池居之常出美玉。熏池未载形，留占位；北望河林及蒨举木比拟存疑，夫诸白鹿四角、洪水兆为古述。','The third Central range begins at Mount Ao-an, with tufu jade on its sunny side and ochre and gold on its shaded side. Xunchi dwells here and produces fine jade. It looks north toward Helin; Fuzhu resembles a white deer with four horns and has an ancient flood omen.','The fine-jade variant gloss spans 71–72. Helin and the qian/ju comparison remain uncertain; no body is invented for Xunchi. Four independent horns are mandatory for Fuzhu.'),
R('r03-qingyao','青要','Mount Qingyao','向东十里为青要，帝之密都，北望河曲南望墠渚。禹父变化、駕鸟疑说、僕纍蒲盧注分别录。武罗人面豹文小腰白齿穿耳鐻，畛水北注河，鴢凫状青身朱目赤尾，荀草形貌与功效另分。','Ten li east is Mount Qingyao, a secluded capital of the emperor, looking north toward a bend of the He and south toward Shanzhu, the transformation site of Yu’s father. Wuluo has a human face, leopard markings, a slim waist, white teeth and pierced ears with ju ornaments. Zhen water flows north into the He and has Yao birds, duck-like with blue-green bodies, red eyes and red tails. Xun grass is also described.','The long account keeps deity, animals, plants and commentary separate. Jia bird is uncertain; snail/insect identifications are commentary. Human body details and the ju ornament shape are artistic. Unit 81 is on scan 10; 82–84 on 11.'),
R('r03-gui','騩山','Mount Wei (Guo Pu pronunciation)','向东十里为騩山，郭注音巍。上美枣阴㻬琈玉，正回水北注河。飞鱼豚状赤文，不以鱼名或飞名添加鳍翼，也不借牛首鲋状飞鱼。','Ten li east is Mount Wei, with fine jujubes above and tufu jade on its shaded side. Zhenghui water flows north into the He. Its Feiyu resemble pigs with red patterns and have ancient eating and protective claims.','Guo Pu glosses the mountain pronunciation by wei. The pig-shaped image has no fish fins or wings; red-pattern geometry and ordinary pig details are artistic.'),
R('r03-yisu','冝蘇','Mount Yisu','向东四十里为冝蘇，上金玉、下蔓居木。滽滽水北注河，多黄贝；蔓居未详，不补现代树种，也不将水名借成东山鱅鱅鱼。','Forty li east is Mount Yisu, with gold and jade above and manju trees below. Yongyong water flows north into the He and has many yellow shells.','Manju is explicitly unknown in commentary. The water stays separate from similarly pronounced waters and fish names elsewhere.'),
R('r03-he','和山','Mount He','向东二十里为和山，无草木、多瑶碧，五曲九水合北注河。泰逢人状虎尾、好居萯山阳；或作雀尾仅异说，不叠画两尾，光及动天地气为古述，长注跨94—95。','Twenty li east is Mount He, without vegetation and with much yaobi. It has five turns and nine waters that unite and flow north into the He. Taifeng is human-shaped with a tiger tail, favors the sunny side of Fu mountain and is described as shining and moving the airs of heaven and earth.','Unit 90 is on scan 11. The alternative bird tail is commentary and is not added to the tiger tail. The Kongjia narrative continues across 94–95.'),
R('r03-summary','次三总括','Third-range summary and rites','次三敖岸至和，五山四百四十里。太逢熏池武罗与一牡羊副、吉玉，另二神雄鸡瘗与稌米分别录。副为破羊骨古礼，不以祭羊形补神躯，不额外造两幅未名神像。','The third range from Ao-an to He contains five mountains and 440 li. Taifeng, Xunchi and Wuluo are associated with one ram and auspicious jade; the other two gods use a buried rooster and rice grain.','The text does not add new anatomy for the named or unnamed gods. The ram-bone gloss describes an ancient rite and is not illustrated as a violent scene.'),
R('r04-luti','鹿蹄','Mount Luti','中次四釐山首鹿蹄，上多玉、下多金。甘水北注洛，水中多泠石，郭注未闻、或作涂；泠石不作现代定种。99在12页末，不误并扶豬。','The fourth Central range begins at Mount Luti, with jade above and gold below. Gan water rises here and flows north into the Luo, with much ling stone.','Unit 99 is on scan 12 and 100 on 13. Commentary says the stone is unknown and records tu as a variant; the range-name pronunciation is separate from Luti.')
]

LINKS = []
SHARES = []


def entities(E):
    LINKS.clear(); SHARES.clear(); out = []; names = {r['slug']: r['name'] for r in ROWS}; en_names = {r['slug']: r['en_name'].removeprefix('Mount ') for r in ROWS}
    def add(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, note='', **extra):
        e = E(s, kind, key, name, en, q, cn, eq, (eq + ' ' + note).strip(), **extra); out.append(e); return e['id']
    def product(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn='只存本段物产及位置，不强定现代种属或成分。', **extra):
        return add(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, 'No unstated modern species, composition or coordinate is inferred.', **extra)
    def water(s, key, name, en, q, eq, cn='本段水名、流向与受水体分别存录，不定现代河道。', **extra):
        return add(s, 'water', key, name, en, q, eq, cn, 'The textual water account does not establish a modern river identity.', **extra)
    def unknown(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, **extra):
        return add(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, 'The form is not independently established; the placeholder does not identify a modern species.', unknown=True, **extra)
    def form(s, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, note, kind='beast', **extra):
        return add(s, kind, key, name, en, q, eq, cn, note, **extra)
    def gj(s, q):
        for key, name, en in [('gold', '金', 'Gold'), ('jade', '玉', 'Jade')]:
            product(s, 'material', key + '-' + s, name + '（' + names[s] + '）', en + ' (' + en_names[s] + ')', q, 'Gold and jade are abundant in this mountain account.')
    def pair(a, b): LINKS.append((a, b))
    s='r01-conglong'
    add(s,'place','valleys-conglong','大谷（葱聾）','Great valleys (Conglong)','其中多大谷','There are many great valleys.','只记大谷泛称，不另造具名行程山或现代坐标。')
    for key,n,en,q in [('white','白堊','White e','白堊'),('black','黑堊','Black e','黑青黄堊'),('blue','青堊','Blue-green e','黑青黄堊'),('yellow','黄堊','Yellow e','黑青黄堊')]:
        product(s,'material',key+'-e-conglong',n+'（葱聾）',en+' (Conglong)',q,'White and black, blue-green and yellow e are recorded; this card isolates one color.','垩色依本段并郭注杂色分别录，不认定为四种现代矿物。',commentary='言有雜色堊也' if key!='white' else '',en_commentary='Guo Pu calls these mixed-color e.' if key!='white' else '')
    for s,q in [('r01-wo','其上多赤銅'),('r01-jianggu','其中多赤銅'),('r01-gudeng','多赤銅'),('r02-kunwu','其上多赤銅')]:product(s,'material','red-copper-'+s,'赤銅（'+names[s]+'）','Red copper ('+en_names[s]+')',q,'Red copper is abundant.')
    product('r01-wo','material','iron-wo','鐵（涹山阴）','Iron (Wo shaded side)','其隂多鐵','Iron is abundant on the shaded side.')
    product('r01-tuohu','plant','zhichu-tuohu','植楮（脱扈）','Zhichu (Tuohu)','有草焉其狀如葵葉而赤華莢實實如㯶莢名曰植楮可以已癙食之不眯','Zhichu has mallow-like leaves, red flowers and zong-like pods, with ancient eating claims.','植楮葵叶赤华荚实；㯶荚比较与癙病音义分开，后者跨17—18，不教导现代用药。',commentary='今㯶木莢似皁莢也；癙病；也淮南子曰狸頭已癙也',en_commentary='Guo Pu compares zong pods with zao pods; the shu-illness gloss continues across units 17–18.')
    product('r01-jinxing','material','tianying-jinxing','天嬰（金星）','Tianying (Jinxing)','多天嬰其狀如龍骨可以已痤','Tianying resembles dragon bones and is said to relieve sores.','未明言草木兽石类别，暂以物产名存录；龙骨只是比拟，不生龙图。',commentary='癰痤也',en_commentary='Guo Pu glosses the ancient ailment.')
    add('r01-taiwei','place','xiaogu-taiwei','梟谷（泰威）','Xiao valley (Taiwei)','其中有谷曰梟谷','There is a valley called Xiao.','梟谷为地名，或无谷字为郭注异说，不指枭鸟。',commentary='或無谷字',en_commentary='Guo Pu records a variant without the valley character.')
    product('r01-taiwei','material','iron-taiwei','鐵（梟谷）','Iron (Xiao valley)','其中多鐵','Iron is abundant in this account.')
    product('r01-wulin','plant','jian-wulin','葌草（吳林）','Jian grass (Wulin)','其中多葌草','Jian grass is abundant.','仅名与写法异说，不借葌山芒草形貌。',commentary='亦菅字',en_commentary='Guo Pu equates the written character with jian grass.')
    product('r01-niushou','plant','gui-niushou','鬼草（牛首）','Gui grass (Niushou)','有草焉名曰鬼草其葉如葵而赤莖其秀如禾服之不憂','Gui grass has mallow-like leaves, red stems and grain-like shoots and is said to avert worry.','鬼据4页影印在阅读层恢复；叶茎秀的比拟逐项录，古述不作药效。')
    lao=water('r01-niushou','lao-niushou','勞水（牛首）','Lao water (Niushou)','勞水出焉而西流注于潏水','The Lao rises here and flows west into the Yu.')
    yu=water('r01-niushou','yu-niushou','潏水（勞水受水体）','Yu water (Lao recipient)','西流注于潏水','It flows west into the Yu.',commentary='音如譎詐之譎',en_commentary='Guo Pu supplies a jue pronunciation comparison.');pair(lao,yu)
    f=form('r01-niushou','feiyu-niushou','飛魚（牛首）','Feiyu (Niushou)','是多飛魚其狀如鮒魚食之已痔衕','Feiyu resemble fu fish and have an ancient eating claim.','飞鱼本段仅如鲋，鱼体四鳍细节、体色姿态为艺术解释，不因飞名添翼，不借豚状赤文。','Ordinary fish details, fin count, colors and pose are artistic; no wings are added.',water=True);pair(lao,f)
    product('r01-huo','plant','gu-huo','榖（霍山）','Gu trees (Huo)','其木多榖','Gu trees are abundant.')
    form('r01-huo','feifei-huo','朏朏（霍山）','Feifei (Huo)','有獸焉其狀如狸而白尾有鬛名曰朏朏養之可以已憂','Feifei resembles a li with a white tail and a mane; keeping it is said to relieve worry.','狸状白尾有鬣据正文，四猫足、鬃形、其余毛色与姿态为艺术解释，不添角翼。','Four feline feet, mane styling, other colors and pose are artistic.',commentary='謂蓄養之也普昧反',en_commentary='Guo Pu explains keeping the animal and gives pronunciation.')
